WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.380
The members of BTS are going to serve in the&nbsp;
military. This is going to cost South Korea&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.380 --> 00:00:09.180
billions of dollars. Billions with a “B.” South&nbsp;
Korea has a law that says that all able-bodied&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.180 --> 00:00:13.560
men must serve in the military. But rich, famous&nbsp;
people have always avoided this through a couple&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:13.560 --> 00:00:17.340
of loopholes. They’ve renounced their citizenship,&nbsp;
they’ve made up health reasons. Oh, and they also&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.340 --> 00:00:21.180
had this entertainment soldier program where&nbsp;
you could get out of serving in the military&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.180 --> 00:00:25.740
by just making propaganda for the military. That&nbsp;
program doesn't exist anymore, by the way. Back&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.740 --> 00:00:29.520
to BTS. They've said that all seven members are&nbsp;
going to serve their two years in the military.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.520 --> 00:00:33.600
So we won't have like BTS K-Pop for a few years?&nbsp;
It's not a big deal, right? No, it's a huge deal.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:39.360
This band brings in around $3.6 billion a year to&nbsp;
South Korea's economy. That's the equivalent of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.360 --> 00:00:45.060
like 26 mid-sized companies combined. This&nbsp;
one band has led to billions of dollars in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.060 --> 00:00:50.760
the sales of cosmetics, clothes, food, oh, and&nbsp;
tourism. 7% of tourists who go to South Korea&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.760 --> 00:00:55.200
say that they go because of BTS. The question&nbsp;
is, why didn't South Korea's government step&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.200 --> 00:00:59.940
in and help BTS get some exemption for serving&nbsp;
in the army? And should they have done that?

